      "indo_pacific_lionfish_were_released_in": "Indo-Pacific lionfish were released in Florida in the 1980s (aquarium trade origin) and exploded across the Caribbean. They have no natural predators in the new range, so reef fish populations have collapsed where lionfish establish. NOAA + REEF.org coordinate citizen-science lionfish removal.",
